00:16:49,834 --> 00:16:51,836
Marshall Johnson,
you owe me money.

257
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,882
I-I'm not the Tesla guy.

258
00:16:53,925 --> 00:16:55,971
Okay? I don't have
that kind of money.

259
00:16:56,058 --> 00:16:57,581
How much money
do you make a year?

260
00:16:57,625 --> 00:16:59,235
What? Uh...

261
00:16:59,279 --> 00:17:01,063
- How much money

262
00:17:01,107 --> 00:17:04,414
do you people in there
make a year?

263
00:17:04,501 --> 00:17:06,982
- I bet you it's more than I do.
- Could you please--

264
00:17:07,069 --> 00:17:10,855
I'm begging you-- could you
please just leave me alone?

265
00:17:10,899 --> 00:17:15,860
That's exactly what
my great-great-grandmother said.

266
00:17:15,947 --> 00:17:17,906
- Marshall Johnson's
great-great-granddaddy

267
00:17:17,949 --> 00:17:20,039
- was a slave owner.
- No, no, no. Not true.

268
00:17:20,082 --> 00:17:23,433
He owned
my great-great-granddaddy.

269
00:17:23,433 --> 00:17:25,218
- Not true.
- You need to pay up!

270
00:17:25,261 --> 00:17:30,440
$3 million.
$3 million.

271
00:17:30,484 --> 00:17:32,790
What do we want? Compensation!

272
00:17:32,790 --> 00:17:35,097
When do we want it? Now!

273
00:17:35,141 --> 00:17:37,665
Marshall Johnson's
great-great-granddaddy

274
00:17:37,708 --> 00:17:39,623
enslaved
my great-great-granddaddy...

275
00:17:40,929 --> 00:17:45,238
Get me a new car,
get Sierra a new car.

276
00:17:45,238 --> 00:17:46,674
You gonna get a Cadillac
or one of them, uh,

277
00:17:46,717 --> 00:17:48,937
- those Cybertrucks?
- I don't know.

278
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:51,113
You know,
Jamal can get a new phone.

279
00:17:51,113 --> 00:17:53,681
Get Tangy and Sierra's mom
a new place,

280
00:17:53,724 --> 00:17:55,900
'cause Lord knows I can't be
dealing with that anymore.

281
00:17:55,944 --> 00:17:59,034
- Her mama?
- You already...

282
00:17:59,121 --> 00:18:01,254
- Hey, Lester?

283
00:18:01,341 --> 00:18:03,256
Could I... could I talk
to you for a sec?

284
00:18:06,041 --> 00:18:07,738
- Yeah. What's up?

285
00:18:07,782 --> 00:18:09,740
Hey, man. How you doing?

286
00:18:09,784 --> 00:18:11,046
- Pretty good.
- Ain't no such thing

287
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:13,179
as free labor, Marshall.

288
00:18:13,266 --> 00:18:16,704
Pay up!

289
00:18:16,747 --> 00:18:19,359
Uh... look,

290
00:18:19,359 --> 00:18:22,405
I know this is a crazy time
and everything,

291
00:18:22,449 --> 00:18:24,973
and, uh, I-I really don't
know what to do.

292
00:18:25,060 --> 00:18:27,758
Uh, no, thanks. Thank you.

293
00:18:27,845 --> 00:18:31,501
Um, I'm just a guy,

294
00:18:31,501 --> 00:18:33,503
you know, trying to get by.

295
00:18:33,547 --> 00:18:39,074
And I feel like this woman
is harassing me, you know?

296
00:18:39,074 --> 00:18:40,902
She's kind of ruining my life.

297
00:18:40,945 --> 00:18:43,209
Uh, so...

298
00:18:43,252 --> 00:18:46,864
I-I just don't know what to do.

299
00:18:46,951 --> 00:18:49,302
You honestly want my advice?

300
00:18:49,345 --> 00:18:51,304
Uh, yes.

301
00:18:51,347 --> 00:18:54,089
Look, man,
I grew up with Black women.

302
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:56,091
Right. I figured.

303
00:18:56,178 --> 00:18:58,441
The only thing you can do is
say you were wrong

304
00:18:58,528 --> 00:19:00,443
and give her as much money
as you can.

305
00:19:00,530 --> 00:19:03,098
She'll probably want to meet
with you one-on-one,

306
00:19:03,098 --> 00:19:04,752
cut you down a bit...

307
00:19:04,795 --> 00:19:06,101
I just don't know what to do.

308
00:19:06,101 --> 00:19:08,538
- Hmm.
- Honestly, my advice?

309
00:19:08,582 --> 00:19:10,801
You got to fight that shit, man.

310
00:19:10,845 --> 00:19:12,673
Come in as hard as her.

311
00:19:12,716 --> 00:19:13,978
- It's the principle.

312
00:19:14,022 --> 00:19:15,763
I looked her up on Instagram.

313
00:19:15,763 --> 00:19:17,634
All she's talking
about is the fact

314
00:19:17,678 --> 00:19:19,549
- that you owe her a lot
of money.

315
00:19:19,593 --> 00:19:21,769
100% Nordic?!

316
00:19:21,769 --> 00:19:23,597
How is that even
fucking possible?

317
00:19:25,773 --> 00:19:28,384
This concerns all of us,
Willy.

318
00:19:28,428 --> 00:19:31,257
No, it don't, Ashley.

319
00:19:33,911 --> 00:19:35,696
No, it don't.

320
00:19:48,709 --> 00:19:50,798
What?

321
00:20:11,862 --> 00:20:13,864
Uh, I was supposed
to pick her up.

322
00:20:13,908 --> 00:20:15,736
What's going on?

323
00:20:17,651 --> 00:20:19,609
Is it true?

324
00:20:19,653 --> 00:20:22,264
Is wh...?

325
00:20:22,264 --> 00:20:25,833
Oh, my God.
Was Sheniqua here?

326
00:20:25,876 --> 00:20:27,835
Did, did she talk to you?

327
00:20:27,878 --> 00:20:29,967
- Marshall, I can't believe you.
- Okay.

328
00:20:30,054 --> 00:20:32,405
Let's just go inside
and discuss this.

329
00:20:32,448 --> 00:20:34,058
Look, you can't come in here.

330
00:20:34,102 --> 00:20:35,843
Seriously, Natalie?

331
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:40,064
Have you checked
your background?

332
00:20:40,108 --> 00:20:41,936
This could have
easily happened to you.

333
00:20:41,936 --> 00:20:44,417
- I'm Peruvian.
This would never happen to me.
- Per...

334
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:46,201
You were white yesterday!

335
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:49,639
Okay, look, Natalie,

336
00:20:49,683 --> 00:20:53,556
please, can we just...
c-can we just go inside

337
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:55,993
and just sit down
and-and just talk about...?

338
00:21:04,480 --> 00:21:08,789
Can I... can I say good night
to Katie?

339
00:21:09,790 --> 00:21:13,533
Marshall...

340
00:21:13,576 --> 00:21:15,448
I can't have my finances
take a hit.

341
00:21:18,189 --> 00:21:20,235
We have
to make the divorce official.

342
00:21:27,242 --> 00:21:28,896
Wait. What?

343
00:21:34,945 --> 00:21:37,644
This is not happening.

344
00:22:04,540 --> 00:22:06,716
What the...?

345
00:22:11,765 --> 00:22:14,202
- There he is!

346
00:22:14,245 --> 00:22:15,638
That's the guy right there.

347
00:22:15,725 --> 00:22:16,900
Oh.

348
00:22:16,944 --> 00:22:19,773
Go get him, Jason!

349
00:22:24,865 --> 00:22:27,084
No, no, no, no.

350
00:22:27,171 --> 00:22:29,652
Oh, shit, shit, shit, shit,
shit, shit, shit.

351
00:22:34,788 --> 00:22:36,529
Oh, my God.

352
00:22:37,051 --> 00:22:38,879
Shit, shit, shit, shit, shit.

353
00:22:40,837 --> 00:22:44,014
Oh, fuck. Oh, fuck. Oh.

354
00:22:54,198 --> 00:22:55,896
Well, sir, you know,
my time was wasted, too...

355
00:23:23,489 --> 00:23:26,709
We didn't do it, but we can
help you get your money.

356
00:23:26,753 --> 00:23:29,190
Don't know if you owe
restitution taxes?

357
00:23:29,233 --> 00:23:32,062
We can help you with that.

358
00:25:13,686 --> 00:25:17,124
Hi. Would you like something
to drink?

359
00:25:17,124 --> 00:25:21,171
Uh, uh, I'll just have
what he's having.

360
00:25:21,258 --> 00:25:22,825
Okay.

361
00:25:33,488 --> 00:25:35,185
How long are you here for?

362
00:25:35,229 --> 00:25:40,364
Honestly,
I am not quite even sure.

363
00:25:40,408 --> 00:25:43,498
Just checked in today.

364
00:25:45,587 --> 00:25:48,503
Yeah, I flew in a few days ago.

365
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:50,592
Looking for a new place.

366
00:25:52,159 --> 00:25:55,075
They can't find my bag, though,
so I look like hell.

367
00:25:59,383 --> 00:26:02,517
Name's Earnest.
Friends call me "E."

368
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:06,739
Marshall.

369
00:26:08,044 --> 00:26:10,873
I have a feeling we're
in the same boat, Marshall.

370
00:26:12,179 --> 00:26:14,660
You owe a lot?

371
00:26:17,053 --> 00:26:21,231
This woman-- she...

372
00:26:21,275 --> 00:26:23,320
follows me everywhere,

373
00:26:23,364 --> 00:26:26,802
won't leave me alone.

374
00:26:26,846 --> 00:26:29,109
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

375
00:26:31,285 --> 00:26:35,681
Just... can't believe
this is actually happening.

376
00:26:39,728 --> 00:26:41,774
Two days ago,
I had a good life,

377
00:26:41,861 --> 00:26:44,777
and now I'm being fucked by
some shit that I didn't even do.

378
00:26:44,820 --> 00:26:48,258
I'm losing my wife, my house,

379
00:26:48,345 --> 00:26:50,347
my daughter.

380
00:26:50,347 --> 00:26:53,002
I don't know.

381
00:26:53,002 --> 00:26:54,917
Didn't fucking do anything.

382
00:27:10,237 --> 00:27:13,022
As I was saying, I don't know.

383
00:27:17,374 --> 00:27:19,420
What?

384
00:27:22,858 --> 00:27:25,513
I don't know.

385
00:27:28,690 --> 00:27:30,692
My grandfather used to tell me

386
00:27:30,692 --> 00:27:34,478
how his father built everything
we had from the ground up,

387
00:27:34,522 --> 00:27:38,395
pulled himself up
by his own bootstraps, you know?

388
00:27:39,396 --> 00:27:42,704
Turns out, he didn't.

389
00:27:42,748 --> 00:27:46,186
Turns out he had a lot of help.

390
00:27:46,273 --> 00:27:48,884
And a lot of kids.

391
00:27:52,148 --> 00:27:53,976
Maybe it's only right.

392
00:27:55,848 --> 00:27:59,982
E, we don't deserve this.

393
00:28:00,069 --> 00:28:02,245
Well, what do they deserve?

394
00:28:06,859 --> 00:28:08,904
We were treating slavery

395
00:28:08,948 --> 00:28:13,779
as if it were a mystery
buried in the past,

396
00:28:13,866 --> 00:28:17,434
something to investigate
if we chose to.

397
00:28:17,521 --> 00:28:21,438
And now that history has
a monetary value.

398
00:28:22,744 --> 00:28:27,444
Confession is not absolution.

399
00:28:29,098 --> 00:28:32,101
And in the case of this
person... What's her name?

400
00:28:32,145 --> 00:28:33,581
Sheniqua.

401
00:28:33,624 --> 00:28:38,107
To Sheniqua, to them...

402
00:28:38,151 --> 00:28:41,110
slavery is not past.

403
00:28:41,154 --> 00:28:44,679
I mean, it's not a mystery.

404
00:28:44,766 --> 00:28:48,248
It is not
an historical curiosity.

405
00:28:48,291 --> 00:28:50,554
It is a cruel,

406
00:28:50,598 --> 00:28:54,080
unavoidable ghost that haunts
in a way we can't see.

407
00:28:55,516 --> 00:28:57,866
None of us are perfect.

408
00:29:03,132 --> 00:29:05,918
So now you're what?
You're separated from your wife?

409
00:29:05,961 --> 00:29:08,050
She's taking your kid?

410
00:29:08,137 --> 00:29:10,836
Now she has to be raised
without a father?

411
00:29:10,923 --> 00:29:13,012
She has to build wealth

412
00:29:13,055 --> 00:29:15,928
and success
from the ground up, right?

413
00:29:15,971 --> 00:29:18,582
It's similar
to the position we put them in.

414
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:23,762
But we're gonna be okay.

415
00:29:27,722 --> 00:29:30,333
Your daughter's gonna be okay.

416
00:29:32,596 --> 00:29:35,382
The curse has been lifted
from her.

417
00:29:37,297 --> 00:29:40,169
All of us--

418
00:29:40,169 --> 00:29:45,174
we were running from it,
but now we're free.

419
00:29:49,483 --> 00:29:51,311
Excuse me.

420
00:30:27,260 --> 00:30:29,436
Come on! Come on, babies!
Come on!

421
00:30:29,479 --> 00:30:31,438
You got it!

422
00:30:31,481 --> 00:30:33,919
Yeah!

423
00:30:34,006 --> 00:30:36,356
Ooh, I'm so proud
of my babies.

424
00:30:53,590 --> 00:30:55,897
Holy shit.

425
00:30:55,897 --> 00:30:57,856
There's more
where that came from.

426
00:32:18,980 --> 00:32:20,895
All right, guys, uh,

427
00:32:20,982 --> 00:32:22,984
I got a decent-sized reservation
in the main dining hall,

428
00:32:23,028 --> 00:32:25,030
so I'm gonna need
all hands on deck for that,

429
00:32:25,073 --> 00:32:27,423
full hands in, full hands out.
You know the routine.

430
00:32:27,423 --> 00:32:30,035
Uh, make sure to push
the daily specials, okay?

431
00:32:30,078 --> 00:32:31,906
I don't want to ask
about that again.

432
00:32:31,993 --> 00:32:34,778
And if anyone has a portion
of their paycheck going

433
00:32:34,778 --> 00:32:37,042
to restitution taxes,
stay after.

434
00:32:37,085 --> 00:32:38,913
Everyone else, hit the floor.

435
00:32:44,832 --> 00:32:47,400
Simon, ten percent?

436
00:32:47,443 --> 00:32:49,402
- One second, please.

437
00:32:49,445 --> 00:32:51,578
Okay, you're good. Thank you.

438
00:32:51,621 --> 00:32:53,580
- Hey.

439
00:32:53,623 --> 00:32:55,364
Uh, name of payee?

440
00:32:55,408 --> 00:32:57,366
Uh, Sheniqua Johnson.

441
00:32:57,410 --> 00:33:00,543
- Okay. And percentage?

442
00:33:00,587 --> 00:33:04,156
- 15%.
- 15%?

443
00:33:04,156 --> 00:33:06,201
Ouch.

444
00:33:07,594 --> 00:33:09,944
Well, at least
tips aren't garnished.

445
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:12,033
There's that.

446
00:33:12,033 --> 00:33:14,862
- Uh, you're good.
- Cool. Thanks.

447
00:33:14,905 --> 00:33:16,777
And you're doing ten again?

448
00:33:31,009 --> 00:33:32,401
Basura blanca.

449
00:33:32,445 --> 00:33:33,663
Hey, huevón.

450
00:33:33,750 --> 00:33:35,448
Get to work.

451
00:33:35,491 --> 00:33:38,668
Te vi llegar tarde, pendejo.

452
00:33:38,755 --> 00:33:41,758
Ah!

453
00:33:41,802 --> 00:33:45,458
Okay. Keep talking like that,
they're gonna make you a busboy.

454
00:34:14,487 --> 00:34:17,403
All right, good evening,
ladies and gentlemen.

455
00:34:19,492 --> 00:34:22,321
- All right.

456
00:34:22,364 --> 00:34:24,236
- Hey.

457
00:34:30,111 --> 00:34:32,026
Okay.

458
00:34:33,636 --> 00:34:35,464
Ooh.
